      "notes_d": [
        {
          "body": "D is the most tempting trap. If placebo subjects got vitamin C from food, the control group was not vitamin-free. But D says only that \"Some\" placebo subjects ate vitamin C-rich foods, which is an ordinary diet and could just as easily describe the vitamin C group. Nothing suggests the food matched the pill's dose or that it happened among the blind subjects. So D barely dents the comparison, while A gives direct evidence that the vitamin helped.",
